      "writtenOn": "2021-02-09T21:58:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since hpd_low always reset\u0027s the queue, then hpd_low can only ever be in the first position. Hpd High can only following hpd_low, and you can\u0027t have hpd_irq without being in hpd_high. So that means in the worst case there can only be 4 events in the queue:\n\nhpd_low -\u003e hpd_high -\u003e hpd_irq -\u003e hpd_irq\n\nIf the queue is full, it must be the situation I just detailed. So that would mean discard. If there are less than 2 events already, then hpd_irq may always be added. The lastly, if there are 2 or more, then don\u0027t add if this would be the 3rd hpd_irq event. That\u0027s what the hpd.queue[hpd.count - 2] \u003d\u003d hpd_irq) is checking for.",
      "parentUuid": "c6bdbe6c_6f834527",
